Warning : Back of the napkin calculations ahead!

With 14 sacks/oilskins, and 3 bags of holding, it should be possible to
nest the bags of holding in such a way that there is only a 13% chance 
(total) of blowing up the bags.  Or, for the optimisits, there is an 
87% chance of not blowing up the bags.  This is assuming you are nesting
the bags all at once.

Assuming the BoHs are all blessed, that will give a 1/64 reduction in
carrying capacity.

A strong character can carry 1000 weight unencumbered, and about 1500 
weight burdened.

A minimal inventory (SDSM, [oMR, Speed Boots, "oLS, + some other items)
will take about 150 weight.  The invocation artifacts are about 50
weight.  The BoH + sacks have a base weight of about 125.  Add another
50 for items-we-don't-want-to-risk-in-the-bag-of-holding, and that's a 
total of 400 or so.

That gives over 1000 for the BoH when burdened, or 600 when unburdened.
When we factor in the holding capacity for the most-nested bag of
holding, that is 64k when burdened, or 38k when unburdened.

Factoring in all artifacts, all unique weapons, armours, potions,
scrolls, wands, amulets, rings, gems, consumables, tools, and one tin 
for every monster in the game (1 gnome, 1 gnome wizard, 1 gnome lord,
etc), the total weight is less then 30k.  [ Excluding 1 of every corpse 
(they are already tinned), and 1 of every statue (too dang heavy). ]

30k is less then 38k, which means it should be possible to ascend with
one of everything in the entire game, without even being burdened.

Scary, huh?

But you have to pick up the first BoH...

Unfortunately, that limits you to 9k.

So, you need roughly 12 - 16 bags of holding (all blessed).

Then 68 sacks.  Plus you have a 44% of needing 1 set of spares, a 35%
chance of needed 2 sets of spares, and a 25% of needed 3 sets of spares, etc.

Since you have a good chance of a few blowing up,  I'd try the artifacts 
and the tins in one bag and hope that the RNG doesn't notice.

Then, find duplicates of the rest, to replace what is lost in the
explosions.

Keep track of what is going into each bag, and you have a good chance of 
succeeding.

Its possible to take it all with you...

